{"id":"be-get-used-to","lv":"b2","n":7,"cat":"verb-patterns","t":"Be used to, get used to: đã quen, dần quen","en":"I'm used to getting up early. · You'll get used to it.","kind":"contrast","sum":"Be used to + danh từ / V-ing = ĐÃ QUEN với: I'm not used to the cold. I'm used to wearing T-shirts. Get used to = DẦN QUEN, trở nên quen: You'll get used to it. It took me a month to get used to driving on the right. To ở đây là giới từ → V-ing (used to getting up, không nói used to get up). Khác hẳn used to + V (thói quen quá khứ): I used to live alone ≠ I'm used to living alone. Cả ba đọc giống nhau /ˈjustə/ — nhìn be / get phía trước để phân biệt.","forms":[{"f":"be used to + danh từ / V-ing = đã quen","vi":"I'm used to the cold."},{"f":"get used to + danh từ / V-ing = dần quen","vi":"You'll get used to it."},{"f":"to là giới từ → V-ing","vi":"I'm used to getting up early."},{"f":"≠ used to + V (thói quen quá khứ)","vi":"I used to live alone."}],"pts":[{"id":"be-get-used-to","name":"be / get used to","vi":"Đã quen / dần quen với: be / get used to + V-ing"}],"cast":{"linh":{"name":{"en":"Linh","vi":"Linh"},"look":"woman","style":{"outfit":"blouse","top":"#9A6FC4","topShade":"#8159AA","accent":"#8159AA","hair":"bob","hairColor":"#1C1716","skin":"#F2CFAE","skinShade":"#E0B592"},"x":1040},"ben":{"name":{"en":"Ben","vi":"Ben"},"look":"man","style":{"outfit":"jacket","top":"#5A6B8C","topShade":"#4A5A78","accent":"#4A5F8F","hair":"short","hairColor":"#B8863B"},"x":560}},"bg":"snow-yard","beats":[{"k":"e","sec":"hook","en":"Linh, how's life in Canada?","vi":"Linh, cuộc sống ở Canada thế nào?","ipa":["lɪn","haʊz","laɪf","ɪn","ˈkænədə"],"who":"ben","ann":{"expression":"happy"},"b":1,"start":0.454,"end":2.144,"timing":[[0,0.454],[1,0.919],[2,1.244],[3,1.519],[4,1.631]]},{"k":"e","sec":"hook","en":"It's great, but I'm not used to the cold yet.","vi":"Tuyệt lắm, nhưng tôi vẫn chưa quen với cái lạnh.","ipa":["ɪts","ɡɹeɪt","bʌt","aɪm","nɑt","just","tu","ðə","koʊld","jɛt"],"who":"linh"